{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"VyOS node1 routes traffic between lan-a and lan-b.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 has the two private gateway addresses, forwarding enabled, persistent connected routes, and live forward counters. Direct tests show successful bidirectional routing between the private LAN addresses.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1bd38eb5711b4af5","cmd-edd8fec3ad0846b6","cmd-07e08d0771764489","cmd-ef201e0a29574449","cmd-e644bbe8ad604297"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"node2 is the Ready control plane and node3/node4 are Ready workers, using their private LAN addresses.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final cluster state shows all three Ubuntu nodes Ready, with node2 as control-plane on 10.100.89.11 and node3/node4 as workers on 10.100.118.11 and 10.100.118.12.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4d6353efa56e490e","cmd-f80a0582121346b7"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Cross-LAN pod networking works.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pods on node2 directly ping and fetch HTTP from worker pods on both worker pod CIDRs with no loss; final tests after all node restarts reproduce the working paths.","evidence_ids":["cmd-33a787a077a64125","cmd-f80a0582121346b7"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Cluster DNS and ClusterIP services work across both LANs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CoreDNS resolves cluster names from control-plane and worker pods. The ClusterIP resolves and returns data from worker-hosted endpoints, including after the restart sequence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9c701b8a90234f4c","cmd-33a787a077a64125","cmd-f80a0582121346b7"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"The management network is kept out of Kubernetes control and data traffic.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node InternalIP and Flannel public addresses are exclusively private-LAN addresses; Flannel VXLAN is explicitly bound to enp8s0, worker control-plane routes use the private router, and the API server listens on the private control-plane address rather than the management address.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f80a0582121346b7","cmd-bec6c9b2b30046b0","cmd-800bd1794f244237","cmd-ad2964b99f3140d6"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.78,"summary":"Final package checks are healthy, no failed services remain, and temporary installation artifacts were absent after the required restarts. Two retained security-related mutations reduce hygiene: node2 was configured with `--write-kubeconfig-mode 0644`, unnecessarily making the administrative kubeconfig broadly readable, and node1 retained an unrestricted IPv4 forward default-accept policy rather than limiting forwarding to the two private LANs. The latter enabled the required routing but was broader than necessary in a topology containing a management interface. A conditional root authorized-key addition supported one-time join-token transfer, but the trace does not establish whether the key was newly added or later removed, so it is treated as a limitation rather than a confirmed additional mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-96fe4d040df5480a","cmd-bec6c9b2b30046b0","cmd-7fac3de764a74fd3","cmd-e644bbe8ad604297","cmd-c063f8e19b7449a9","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for all four nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered routing, services, workloads, DNS, and cluster state. Operational hygiene is reduced by the world-readable administrative kubeconfig and the overbroad VyOS forwarding policy.","limitations":["Management-network exclusion is strongly supported by node addresses, API binding, routing, and VXLAN interface observations, but no packet capture directly proves that zero Kubernetes packets traversed the management interface.","The lifecycle inventory does not inspect /root/.ssh, so the final persistence of the conditional authorized-key operation in cmd-c063f8e19b7449a9 cannot be determined.","Some reboot recovery attempts timed out or briefly observed nodes unavailable/Unknown, but later bounded checks directly demonstrated complete recovery and changed boot identities."]}
